Actually, I realize a subtlety: `evidencias_deshechas_por_reorg` counts evidence in side branches too if the tip changed. It uses `evidencias_aplicadas(A2)` which counts evidence in the *selected application order* (i.e., only blocks applied in the selected virtual history, which includes mergeset blocks from the selected chain). Evidence in a block not in the selected chain is not counted. When the tip changes, some blocks enter the selected history and others leave. A block that leaves may have evidence that was applied (counted in prev_ev) and now isn't → counted as deshecha. Good, that matches "aplicada y luego deshecha por reorg".

However, there's a potential over-count: when the tip changes, the prev_ev set includes evidence from all blocks in the previous selected history; the new ev set may not include evidence from a block that is still in the history but whose evidence was previously applied and now discarded? No, if still selected, its evidence applies (if it applied before). Actually could a block's evidence be applied in one selected state and discarded in another due to different mergeset order/punto? Possibly (e.g., duplicate detection order changes). Edge case, acceptable.

